1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,700
I asked my coding agent to give

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:03,860
the top bar a bit more room.

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,640
Two lines of CSS.

4
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:07,760
Then it runs selfie render.

5
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,940
That renders all 142 stories in a pinned container,

6
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:15,360
right here on this MacBook Air, in under 30 seconds,

7
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:18,220
with no cloud and no bill per image.

8
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:19,700
Now it’s my turn.

9
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,740
The selfie ui command shows me what changed:

10
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:25,520
those two lines touched every story.

11
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,100
But Selfie has already found the

12
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,080
changes repeated across them.

13
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,960
I look through them, accept them,

14
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:34,300
and 63 of the 142 are done.

15
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,180
But what about dark mode?

16
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:38,560
I search for dark, and there it is:

17
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,240
85,000 changed pixels.

18
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:44,000
Press F, and the images swap in place.

19
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,700
The top bar went white.

20
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:47,680
Selfie can tell me exactly which

21
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:50,160
pixels changed, but not why.

22
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:51,640
The commit is on GitHub,

23
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:54,000
so I open the same story in the cloud,

24
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,420
and ask Muse Spark what caused it.

25
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:59,180
It reads the before, the after, the diff,

26
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:01,740
and the code, and it finds the line.

27
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,940
Then it spots what I never asked for:

28
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:07,200
a fixed light color, where the theme’s color used to be.

29
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,460
It even tells me to check dark mode.

30
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,940
So back in my review, I click the change, write a note,

31
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,460
and send it to the agent, which has been waiting.

32
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:17,880
It gets my words, the exact box,

33
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,800
and a picture of what I saw.

34
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,580
It puts the theme’s color back,

35
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:24,000
renders again, and answers my note.

36
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,780
The bar is dark again, and 85,000

37
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:29,480
changed pixels are down to 13.

38
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,260
I approve the rest, and the agent

39
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:33,320
commits and reviews once more.

40
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:36,440
It’s the exact same build, so nothing renders.

41
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:39,260
Under half a second, and exit 0.

42
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,700
Selfie works with any coding agent.

43
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,940
If you have a Storybook,

44
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:44,660
you can start locally today,

45
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,460
and the link’s in the description.
